+   opcode field can't hold this extra byte itself since it stores at most
+   one prefix byte + one final opcode byte, so instructions using these
+   maps must pass OPC_0F explicitly too (see the aes-ni entries in
+   x86_64-asm.h) rather than relying on the usual embedded-0x0f-literal
+   auto-detect in the O()/T() macros below. */
